<title>Netherlands: TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROSMALEN, Netherlands 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the Heineken Trophy tennis tournament on Friday (prefix number denotes seed):</p>
<p>Men's quarter finals:</p>
<p>1-Michael Chang (U.S.) beat 8-Francisco Clavet (Spain) 6-7</p>
<p>(5-7) 7-6 (10-8) 6-1</p>
<p>4-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Fernon Wibier (Netherlands) 6-2</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Guillaume Raoux (France) beat Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-5) 6-4</p>
<p>Add men's quarter finals: 3-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Martin Damm (Czech Republic) 7-6 (7-5) 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Women's semifinals: 3-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat 8-Asa Carlsson (Sweden) 6-4 6-2 1-Anke Huber (Germany) and Miriam Oremans (Netherlands) leval 6-4 4-6 (suspended because of rain, play resumes on Saturday)</p>
</text>
